        "math_academy_id": "q-341146",
        "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for $f(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot arccot\\,x.$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}\\cdot arccot\\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})\\cdot arccot\\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
        "deliberately_incorrect_submission": false,
